taskDescriptions.prepare_coa_sync='Default output is structured differences, issues, warnings and preview pagination. Excel export is optional. Accept friendly rows from an uploaded Excel (name, code, group; Report BS/PL and Type Account/Group only needed to classify new items). Use rows OR items, up to 2000. Match case/space-insensitive codes and names, ignoring a code prefix in names. Resolve ambiguous matches using issue candidates. Preparation performs no Manager writes. Prepare an immutable add/update COA sync from up to 2000 desired items. Match explicit item_key, otherwise unique code, otherwise exact name within kind. Unmatched items create ordinary BS/P&L accounts or groups. set.group_ref refers to an input ref, including new groups. New items need name and group; For PL groups, group_type is 0 Income, 1 Expense, 2 Subgroup of. A parent implies Type 2; top-level groups require explicit Type 0 or 1 and group_key:null. Existing PL group type changes are previewed. Omitted items are retained. No Manager writes. Show the entire create/update/unchanged preview and cycle-path warnings for approval.';
taskDescriptions.execute_coa_sync='Execute only the exact fully previewed, explicitly user-approved COA sync with task_id and approval_hash. Up to 200 items per call (default 200), with an adaptive response window to return saved progress before the observed MCP timeout. This is not a total task time limit; continue the same approved task until finished. Slow items may still exceed the connection timeout; read and reconcile before resuming. Automatically continue the same approved task while in_progress, without another user approval for each chunk. Caller must remain active; this is not an unattended background job. Creates parents first, verifies writes, checks conflicts, and resumes the same task. Never retries succeeded or uncertain items. Partial completion is possible; no automatic rollback.';
